# What the build must not carry.
#
# `node_modules` above all: the image installs its own for the right
# platform, and copying the host's both bloats the context and risks
# binaries built for another architecture.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.git

# Secrets. An image with the production `.env` baked in is a secret in
# every registry it is pushed to, and `.env` is the one file whose contents
# are supposed to come from the deployment rather than the build.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Uploads, backups and local state: data, not code — and a dump in the
# build context is every workspace's data in the image.
.storage
server/.storage
backups
*.dump
tuff-files-*

# Test leavings, which are large and worthless to the image.
test-results
playwright-report

# Documentation and tooling the running product never reads.
docs
.github
*.md
!README.md
